target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestReportProbeReportsBothAnswers'
expect: a_refused_run_id_is_attributable
why:    a refused run id and an unrunnable probe are different facts. The id was well-formed enough to answer and the answer is no, so the refusal has a stateable cause; conflating it with "could not ask" is the wrong fact about the wrong repair. The value is unobservable through EVERY current caller — Check rejects an invalid run id with an error before reportProbe is reached (measured: `-run-id '../escape'` exits 1 with empty stdout and no diagnosis), and ReportLanded discards the second value and has no production caller — which is exactly why this needs a direct reportProbe test and why the cost is borne by the next caller that reads it. An earlier version of this line claimed the flip makes Check emit the diagnosis blaming a missing gh/git; Check cannot reach that state. Reproduced: this exact flip left the whole package green.
--- old
		return false, true
	}
	needles := append([]string{fmt.Sprintf(reportMarker, runID)}, Fingerprint(r)...)
--- new
		return false, false
	}
	needles := append([]string{fmt.Sprintf(reportMarker, runID)}, Fingerprint(r)...)
